    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Luis Robert Jr.**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 76.18. Facing a favorable matchup against Bennett (xERA 3.99), **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits from a dynamic platoon advantage and a high-probability base-stealing environment created by Bennett\u2019s slow delivery. We are also leaning heavily into our infield power today; **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.93) and **Coby Mayo** (66.72) are our most reliable anchors. **Coby Mayo** in particular gains massive value from the park factor and the opportunity to hit out of the two-hole, while **Gunnar Henderson** rounds out the top-tier plays with a 63.75 score, bolstered by his ability to capitalize on the same pitcher\u2019s lack of urgency on the mound to secure a crucial stolen base.\n\nWhile **Henry Bolte** (64.99) secures a start due to a significant SP skill advantage against Anderson (xERA 5.25), our bench depth remains a point of focus. With **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** unavailable due to injury or scheduling, the decision to sit depth pieces like **Jacob Wilson** or **Drake Baldwin** was clear-cut, as they currently lack the high-leverage platoon matchups enjoyed by our active starters. We are keeping a close watch on **Miguel Vargas** (52.56) and **Sam Antonacci** (57.09); while they are our \"marginal\" starts today against Brown, their high recency metrics and favorable batting order positions make them viable for maintaining our daily efficiency targets. We remain cautiously optimistic that the volatility surrounding Bennett's delivery will yield the stolen base production necessary to keep pace in a competitive Roto landscape.",
